       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the normal maximum single dose of 1000 mg. At 15 g/day, the risk of acute liver injury and liver failure is high, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these common regimens?\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO three times daily** (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intended, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 5000 mg, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist first."
      }
