      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a potentially lethal dose. It could cause serious liver injury, and the patient would get no benefit from it.\n\nI'm not willing to place it, even with confirmation from a student. A medical student's confirmation isn't the review this needs. Please take it to your supervising resident or attending. If a prescriber really intends this dose, they should talk it through with pharmacy first. I don't expect either of them to approve it.\n\nIf you meant a standard dose, I can enter one now:\n- 650 mg PO three times daily\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), which is a common maximum for scheduled dosing\n\nIf you give me one of these doses, or another dose within the safe range, I'll enter it right away."
      }
